From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:27:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: add g16_rwork_pack to keep render
 work blocks back to back

Each render pass slot has its TA work block and its FS work block in
pages of their own, one pass slot window apart. The macOS driver keeps
the TA work blocks of consecutive render commands 0x940 apart and the
FS work blocks 0xcc0 apart (the 0xca0 block rounded up to 64 bytes),
each kind in one buffer.

With g16_rwork_pack=1 a VM's render units keep their TA and FS work
blocks that way in one buffer after the compute work blocks of
g16_cwork_pack, one TA block and one FS block per unit, units built
later included. The work rings, the records and the per-use scrub name
the packed blocks; the per-slot pages are left unused.

The switch is read once, when the first render units are built, so
every VM of a boot is laid out the same way. The default of 0 keeps
the per-slot pages.

Assisted-by: LLM
